# Tic-Tac-Toe Game (Python)

## Project Overview

Tic-Tac-Toe is a simple two-player, console-based game developed using Python. Players take turns placing X and O on a 3×3 game board. The first player to match three symbols horizontally, vertically, or diagonally wins the game.

If all nine cells are filled without a winner, the game ends in a draw.

## Features

- Two-player gameplay.
- 3×3 game board.
- Player 1 uses X and Player 2 uses O.
- Players select cells using numbers from 1 to 9.
- Input validation for incorrect entries.
- Prevents players from selecting occupied cells.
- Automatic winner detection.
- Draw detection.
- Option to play again.

## Technologies Used

- **Programming Language:** Python 3
- **Interface:** Command Line Interface (CLI)
- **Concepts:** Functions, Lists, Loops, Conditional Statements and User Input.

